  "notes": "Agent re-read after the Code Health refactor, 2026-11-07, under the owner directive transcribed in verification/reviews/rulings/agent-rereview-after-refactor-2026-11-07.md. This record is NOT an owner signature: it attests the agent's substantive reading only. Read proxy.serving_identity_provenance. tls.rs became tls/{peer,delegated,options,request_guard,fault_accept_any,mod}.rs: a sorted-line comparison of the old file against the new tree shows the resolver chain moved verbatim; served_channel_peer keeps the signature (accepted evidence, options, request, now) with no second credential parameter and still ends in resolve_channel_peer, whose body is unchanged. Both serving paths still call it once per request: async_serve and blocking_mtls_harness changed only to take the clock from crate::clock::now_unix, ServerOptions::target as a RequestTarget, ServedLimits and ConnectionBounds instead of one ServerLimits, and the Content-Length scan moved into content_length_values; none of that touches where identity or currency comes from. serving_identity_provenance_test.rs changed one line (DISPATCH_MODULE now tls/peer.rs); scripts/serving_identity_provenance_gate.py was restructured into named helpers with the same clauses (resolver defined, no forbidden parameter, each link reaches its authority, no raw-representation route, the online_ocsp residue clause) and passes on this tree. The claim, scope and premises are unchanged. Evidence class as registered; V0 units are tested and probed, not machine-checked proofs. The mutation lane was not re-run by this reading; check-registries resolves every probe anchor.",
